{
 "name": "triangulate_convex_strip_divergence",
 "face_ring_start": "compared",
 "description": "Task 1320. These four cells used to DECLARE a gap: the reference's bare triple command runs a convex-only zig-zag STRIP, and task 1280 had ported only the ear CLIP -- which is that strip's own fallback -- so on every convex ring the two engines parted company. Task 1320 ported the strip, so the gap is CLOSED and every case here declares an EMPTY one, which this runner asserts exactly as strictly as a non-empty one: our live output must equal the frozen reference output, tuple for tuple. The quad is still the load-bearing case. At four corners the strip and the clip emit the same two triangles with the same winding across the same diagonal, differing only in where each tuple STARTS -- so a rotation-tolerant channel reads the quad as parity whether or not the port landed, and only `face_tuples` witnesses which path ran. Every case now carries that channel, which is why `face_ring_start` is \"compared\" here where task 1310 had to record \"ignored\": the ring-set channel is no longer the only one on the n>=5 cases, and our rings now match the frozen ones start-and-all rather than up to rotation.",
